{"raw": {"https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205154": {"title": "Administrative Assistant", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: Administrative Assistant - Performing Arts & Theatre Institute at Sage Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: Administrative Assistant - Performing Arts & Theatre Institute at Sage Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Administrative Assistant - Performing Arts & Theatre Institute at Sage Category: Staff Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Performing Arts Locations: Troy, NY Posted: Sep 24, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position\u00a0ID: 205154 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge. Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: This administrative assistant supports the faculty and staff of the Performing Arts department and the Theatre Institute at Sage (TIS) in the daily operation of an active department, specifically focused on the Troy campus supporting the Theater and Musical Theater programs (collectively referred to as The Theatre Institute at Sage). The position provides the following administrative support: Scheduling of space for student use, campus events, and external rentals Maintaining of department budgets Purchasing of supplies Processing reimbursements and payments Hiring, training, and supervising work study students The position also supports the Theatre Institute at Sage, the college's educational theatre company in the following capacities: Occasional weekend and night shifts to manage the box office Familiarity with POS systems is ideal (TouchNet, Clover) Assisting in the designing, development, and distribution of posters, programs, and press releases Overseeing and training work study students to be Box Office and Front of House staff for shows Requesting and completing show licensing contracts The estimated wage is $19.25\u00a0per hour for 37.5 hours per week for 52\u00a0weeks (12 months). Requirements: A successful candidate will also have the following skills: Highly effective organizational skills A positive attitude and ability to collaborate with others Professionalism Self-motivation and ability to work independently Experience with parts of the Adobe Design suite (Photoshop, Publisher, Express) and website design Previous experience working in a theatre environment (A B.A. in Theatre Arts or Business/Management) Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications accepted until position is filled. Reports to: Program Director of the Musical Theatre Department Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Resume Cover letter A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205200": {"title": "Major Gifts Officer", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: Major Gifts Officer Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: Major Gifts Officer Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Major Gifts Officer Category: Administrative Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Advancement Locations: Troy, NY Posted: Sep 25, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position\u00a0ID: 205200 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge. Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: Position Summary The Major Gifts Officer (MGO) plays a pivotal role in advancing the mission and priorities of the College. Responsible for managing a portfolio of 100 high-net-worth prospective donors- including alumni, parents, and friends of the college- the MGO will identify, qualify, cultivate, solicit, and steward major gifts (typically $25,000+). In a tight-knit campus community of ~3,500 students, this role requires a strategic, highly collaborative fundraiser who thrives on building authentic, long-term relationships and can articulate the unique impact of a private, student-centered education. Key Responsibilities 1. Portfolio Management & Frontline Fundraising (70%) Maintain an active portfolio of approximately 100 major gift prospects. Conduct 10-12 substantive personal donor interactions (in-person visits, virtual meetings, or intentional calls) per month. Develop tailored strategy plans for each prospect, moving them deliberately through the donor pipeline: qualification to cultivation to solicitation to stewardship. Solicit and secure major gifts for capital projects, endowed scholarships, academic programs, and the annual fund. Primary liaison for major gifts that support the Denise Tabor Finard '80 Women's Institute. Collaborate with Executive Director of Gift Planning to incorporate blended gift opportunities (bequests, trusts, annuities) when appropriate. 2. Campus & Strategic Engagement (15%) Partner closely with faculty, department chairs, athletic leaders, and senior leadership (including the President and Vice President) to align donor passions with institutional priorities. Brief executive leadership and draft strategic talking points prior to major prospect meetings or regional donor events. Attend key campus traditions (Reunion, Commencement, Local and Regional Alumni Gatherings) to engage prospects organically. 3. Administration & Data Integrity (15%) Document all donor interactions, contact reports, strategies, and proposals in the advancement CRM database in a timely manner. Track monthly and annual progress toward personal activity and fundraising goals. Participate in advancement team meetings, prospect management sessions, and campaign planning. The estimated salary range is $78,000 to $86,000 per year for 40 hours per week for 52\u00a0weeks (12 months). Requirements: Qualifications & Requirements Education: Bachelor's degree required. Experience: 3-5 years of successful fundraising experience, ideally in higher education or a non-profit setting, with a proven track record of closing major gifts ($25,000+). Travel: Willingness and ability to travel frequently (approximately 30-40% regional travel, primarily in NY, New England, and the Tri-State area). Communication: Exceptional written, verbal, and interpersonal skills; ability to tell compelling stories about the value of a liberal arts education. Tech-Savvy: Proficiency with advancement databases/CRMs (e.g., Raiser's Edge, Salesforce, Slate) and Microsoft Office. Ideal Candidate Profile What makes someone succeed at Russell Sage College: Adaptability & Initiative: You don't mind wearing multiple hats or helping out at events when needed. Authentic Community Connection: You appreciate a small campus culture where you can drop by a professor's office or grab coffee with a coach to understand what needs funding. Regional Familiarity: Knowledge of the Upstate NY philanthropic landscape and regional alumni pockets is a strong plus. Work Environment & Location Location: On-campus (Upstate NY) with flexibility for hybrid work during non-travel weeks, depending on department policy. Working Conditions: Requires regular evening/weekend work for events and donor travel. Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications accepted until position is filled. Reports to:\u00a0Senior Director of Major Gifts Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Resume Cover letter A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205245": {"title": "Administrative Office Coordinator, Undergraduate Nursing", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: Administrative Office Coordinator, Undergraduate Nursing Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: Administrative Office Coordinator, Undergraduate Nursing Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Administrative Office Coordinator, Undergraduate Nursing Category: Staff Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing Locations: Troy, NY Posted: Sep 25, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Hourly Position\u00a0ID: 205245 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge. Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: The on-site full-time\u00a0Administrative Office Coordinator for Undergraduate Nursing collaborates with the remote part-time administrative office coordinator for undergraduate nursing. The coordinator reports to the Administrative Coordinator for Graduate Nursing and the Chair of Nursing. The coordinator supports the nursing program in meeting the needs of the nursing students, faculty, institution, and external partners by initiating, establishing, and maintaining clinical contracts and all related documents; and by maintaining ongoing communication with all stakeholders. The undergraduate nursing office coordinator\u00a0coordinates with faculty and the\u00a0graduate nursing coordinator with placement, confirmation, and communication regarding students in clinical and lab sites-\u00a0including student documentation related to orientation, health clearance, completion of mandatory orientation modules, and health clearance.\u00a0 This includes the creation, maintenance and oversight with faculty regarding student placement. In addition, this position also collaborates with the remote undergraduate coordinator and the faculty to ensure all agencies provide the appropriate experiences for students to achieve course, program, and NY State Ed and accreditation outcomes. The Administrative Office Coordinator for Undergraduate Nursing will also assist undergraduate and graduate office coordinators and faculty to identify, track, and record requirements at each clinical placement site (such as orientation mandatories including completion of modules, pre- and post-tests) and communicate these clinical requirements to instructor and student groups in a timely manner.\u00a0 Additional responsibilities include overseeing database management and records management, communicating effectively to meet the needs of faculty and students, placing service tickets and work orders, assisting with reports- including appendices and virtual resources- and as needed with annual NYSED and AACN reports. The estimated wage\u00a0is $20 per hour for 37.5 hours per week for 52\u00a0weeks (12 months). Requirements: Baccalaureate Degree Preferred; will consider comparable training and experience Advanced verbal and written communication skills Advanced Skills in Microsoft Suite including Excel and all of Google Workspace Previous office experience and ability to make informed decisions in a fast-paced setting Ability to organize and complete projects with or without supervision are essential Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications accepted until position is filled. Reports to: Chair of the Nursing Department Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Resume Cover letter A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205518": {"title": "Assistant Professor of the Practice of Biology", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of the Practice of Biology Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of the Practice of Biology Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of the Practice of Biology Category: Faculty Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Biology Locations: Troy, NY Posted: Oct 5, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position\u00a0ID: 205518 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge. Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: The undergraduate Biology and Health Sciences department at Russell Sage College invites applications for a 9-month, full-time faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Practice for the fall of 2027. The successful applicant will possess an academic doctorate (PhD or equivalent) in the Biological Sciences. Primary responsibilities include teaching lectures and laboratories in microbiology. Additional teaching responsibilities may include research methods, or upper-level courses based on the candidate's specialization. Prior undergraduate teaching experience in these areas will enhance the candidate's application. A successful candidate will be able to mentor research students in addition to teaching.\u00a0 All faculty in the department advise students beginning their second year at Russell Sage College under the guidance of a mentor. All courses offered by the department will be delivered in person. Candidates should anticipate that they will be teaching seven courses over the academic year. The estimated base academic year salary range for this position is $53,000- $57,000, commensurate with experience. Requirements: The successful applicant will possess an academic doctorate (PhD or equivalent) in the Biological Sciences. Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications accepted until position is filled. Reports to: Chair of the Department of Biology & Health Sciences Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Curriculum vitae Letter of Intent Statement of teaching philosophy A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205521": {"title": "Administrative Assistant - Psychology", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: Administrative Assistant - Psychology Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: Administrative Assistant - Psychology Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Administrative Assistant - Psychology Category: Staff Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Psychology Locations: Troy, NY Posted: Oct 5, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Hourly Position\u00a0ID: 205521 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge. Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: The Department of Psychology at Russell Sage College (RSC) invites applications for a part-time (50%) Administrative Assistant. This position provides administrative support for the department's graduate programs, with priority given to counseling internship and Community Psychology externship needs. Responsibilities include: Preparing, routing, and tracking internships/practicum contracts, student documentation, and required forms; monitoring deadlines and following up on missing items. Maintaining current placement records and site contact information, assisting with scheduling, and coordinating routine communications with students and site supervisors. Assisting with the management and review of graduate student and alumni files, including records of student progress and completion of placement requirements. Supporting graduate program data collection, student events, and related departmental activities, with placement administration taking priority. The assistant will collaborate with departmental staff, faculty, and the clinical coordinator to maintain accurate records and support timely completion of administrative requirements. The estimated wage\u00a0is $23.07per hour for 18.75\u00a0hours per week for 52\u00a0weeks. Requirements: The successful candidate will possess a high school diploma or equivalent; strong organizational, written, and verbal communication skills; data and file management experience; and proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and/or Google Workspace. Attention to detail, the ability to manage multiple deadlines, and discretion in handling confidential student records are essential. Preferred qualifications include a college degree, experience working in a college setting, and familiarity with CourseLeaf, Colleague, Canvas, or other academic operations software. Experience supporting internships, field placements, or similar administrative processes is also preferred. Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications accepted until position is filled. Reports to: Chair of the Psychology Department Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Resume Cover letter A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=201760": {"title": "Assistant Vice President of Finance", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: Assistant Vice President of Finance Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Vice President of Finance Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Vice President of Finance Category: Administrative Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Financial Affairs Locations: Troy, NY Posted: Jun 22, 2026 Closes: Jan 29, 2027 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 201760 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge. Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: Overview The Assistant Vice President of Finance (AVP) reports to the Vice President for Finance and Administration. The AVP is responsible for supervising Finance department staff and activity; providing leadership over financial management and reporting; and establishing an effective internal controls framework through accounting policies and procedures to ensure Russell Sage College's financial resources and systems are utilized prudently and in compliance with external financial regulations. The AVP serves as a working manager for a broad range of financial and support operations, including controller functions, auditing, budgeting, and investment management. In the period leading up to the anticipated completion of the merger with ACPHS on or about July 1, 2027, subject to regulatory approvals, the AVP will be expected to work collaboratively with colleagues across both institutions to advance shared priorities, support strategic alignment, and ensure a thoughtful and effective transition. Responsibilities Serve as the senior advisor on all matters related to the financial reporting of the College. Serve as the liaison for the College's external audit firm, external investment managers, tax and financial consultants, actuaries, and bankers. Oversee accounting (including accounts payable, collections, and procurement), budget, and payroll functions of the College. Coordinate the annual audit of the College's financial statements, including review of work papers and financial statements. Coordinate and prepare the College's federal tax returns (annual forms 990 and 5500). Assure compliance with generally accepted accounting principles and auditing standards. Assure compliance with federal and state regulations, including tax compliance. Develop, implement, and maintain accounting, reporting, data, and internal control systems responsive to the College's managerial and fiduciary needs. Prepare financial reports and detailed financial analysis. Provide forecasting and modeling for projects as directed by the Vice President. Manage the development, implementation, and revision of the College's accounting policies and procedures. Conduct internal audits and notify the Vice President of any suspected irregularities against approved policies and procedures. Manage treasury functions daily. Assist with budget development, implementation, and monitoring. Oversee long-term debt repayment schedules and equipment lease programs. Provide financial consult on all major grants and manage financial requirements of construction projects. Oversee administration of retirement plans for compliance and management of audit. Review the quarterly reconciliation of endowment and life income funds, including the distribution of income and unit share calculations. Conduct and/or supervise training for all functions of the Finance office. Assist other College departments with financial transactions and analysis. Facilitate team building and staff development. Partner with the College's Management Information System (MIS) department to ensure the technology needs of the Finance office are met in a cost-effective manner. Assist the Vice President with reporting and analysis for various Board of Trustees committees and subcommittees in the areas of finance/organizational sustainability, audit, and investment. The estimated salary range is between $130,000 and $140,000 per year for 40 hours per week for 52 weeks. Requirements: Qualifications This position requires a finance professional whose background is characterized by initiative, leadership, well-refined organization skills, and proven expertise in the field of financial management. The successful candidate will be an individual who wants to make a difference and actively participate in the long-range goals of Russell Sage College. This position requires: A bachelor's degree and Certified Public Accountant (CPA) license A minimum of seven (7) years of progressively responsible and related experience, preferably in higher education Broad-based experience in finance and accounting, financial reporting, and endowment management A demonstrated record of effective financial management An ability to effectively present information, develop new programs, maintain high quality services, and leverage information technology to perform responsibilities Skills Extensive knowledge of fiscal management, financial reporting, nonprofit and gift accounting, and fiscal forecasting and planning within a college or university setting. Experience in the use of Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) systems and Microsoft Office Suite. Substantial experience and demonstrated competence in the use of financial reporting/modeling tools, financial reporting requirements at the state and federal levels, and conceptualizing and implementing business and operational efficiencies within an organization. Ability to collaborate effectively and communicate tactfully with the College community. Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications accepted until position is filled. Reports to: Vice President for Finance and Administration Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Resume Cover letter A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=201686": {"title": "Assistant Professor of the Practice of Education", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of the Practice of Education Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of the Practice of Education Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of the Practice of Education Category: Faculty Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Education Locations: Troy, NY Posted: Jun 18, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position\u00a0ID: 201686 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge. Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: The Department of Professional Education Programs of The Esteves School of Education at Russell Sage College invites applications for a full-time, professor of practice (non-tenure track)\u00a0 faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Education, effective for Academic Year 2026/2027. The candidate will be responsible for teaching graduate courses in our Literacy Specialist graduate degree program, as well as courses, as needed, in additional graduate programs and/or undergraduate education programs within the Esteves School of Education. In addition, as is typical of positions in higher education, the successful candidate will serve as advisor to program majors, partner with key stakeholders for recruitment and retention endeavors, and maintain scholarship/professional accomplishment (Boyer Model). Location: in-person/hybrid (some in-person, some remote). The estimated base academic year salary for this position is $55,000, commensurate with experience. Requirements: The successful candidate will have an earned terminal degree (PhD, EdD) in literacy or a related area (ABD may be considered based on degree completion timeline and applications) or significant professional experience (15-20+ years). The applicant should have current knowledge and practice on multiple approaches to preparing teachers to engage students in literacy (must have experience with the Science of Reading and other methodologies). Preferred: In addition to the minimum requirements, the preferred candidate will have successful experience teaching in higher education with a variety of modalities, including online asynchronous courses, professional experience, and a network that applies directly to the degree program. Ideal candidate has a blend of PK-12\u00a0and higher education teaching experience and leadership capabilities. Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications accepted until position is filled. Reports to: Chair, Department of Professional Education Programs Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Resume Cover letter A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=161859": {"title": "Assistant Professor of the Practice or Lecturer of Nursing", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of the Practice or Lecturer of Nursing Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of the Practice or Lecturer of Nursing Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of the Practice or Lecturer of Nursing Category: Faculty Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing Locations: Troy, NY Posted: May 2, 2023 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position\u00a0ID: 161859 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge.\u00a0Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: Candidates may apply for a full or half-time (50% FTE) Assistant Professor of Nursing Practice position for the Baccalaureate Faculty Position with a Doctorate preferred and/or Lecturer in Nursing with a\u00a0Master's Degree in Nursing.\u00a0The estimated base academic year salary range for this position will be based on the level offered and\u00a0commensurate with experience. **\u00a0Applications are reviewed on an ongoing basis ** Russell Sage College's Department of Nursing is a well-established program with over 600 students and a rich 101-year history of excellence and innovation in nursing. Nursing programs of study are offered at the Undergraduate, Graduate and Doctoral levels. Requirements: Preference will be given to candidates for Baccalaureate Nursing Faculty with A\u00a0current Doctorate in Nursing degree or MS Degree in Nursing; Hybrid or Online Graduate teaching experience and; Current NYS RN nursing license. Other preferred experiences include current online or web-enhanced teaching, curriculum development, research experience, and leadership in advancing healthcare and/or community service. Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere along with opportunities for tuition waiver, employer matched retirement plan for eligible employees and many other benefits.\u00a0 For complete employee benefit information, please visit our Employee Benefits page. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications are reviewed on an ongoing basis Reports to: Chair of the Nursing department Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Curriculum vitae Letter of intent Academic transcripts Recent evidence of scholarship Copies of professional license(s) Registration and national certification(s) A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=200636": {"title": "Electrician", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: Electrician Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: Electrician Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Electrician Category: Staff Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Locations: Albany, NY Posted: May 18, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Non-Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 200636 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge. Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: RESPONSIBILITIES: Installs, maintains and repairs electrical wiring, conduit, equipment and devices, including complex instrumentation and campus wide DDC control systems Installs, tests, maintains and troubleshoots telecommunications equipment and wiring Responsible for adding, moving and changing of telephone lines, data lines, and equipment Responsible for testing, maintaining, and troubleshooting cable TV up to the service Responsible for preventive and corrective maintenance on all HVAC equipment and exhaust fans Responsible for periodic testing, maintenance, reporting, and repair of all fire alarm systems and associated peripherals Reads, interprets, and follows architectural drawings, schematics/blueprints, sketches, and specifications Responsible to follow all standards and prescribed electrical code and other safety regulations such as Lockout/Tagout Performs electrical maintenance in accordance with manufacturers installation and maintenance documentation and/or verbal instructions Completes special projects as assigned Other responsibilities as assigned by the Crew Coordinator, Assistant Directors, or Senior Director DUTIES: Repairs, installs, replaces and maintains electrical circuits, equipment and appliances, including high voltage and DC circuits Inspects, tests and performs preventive and corrective maintenance of electrical equipment, lighting, signal, HVAC, communications and power circuits Troubleshoots and isolates defects in wiring, switches, motors, lighting, \u00a0DDC controls, and other electrical equipment using appropriate test instruments such as an ammeter, ohm meter, volt meter, test lamp, megger, \u00a0prowler, or signal generator Performs periodic testing, maintenance, reporting, and repair of all fire alarm systems and associated peripherals Troubleshoots, repairs, and maintains emergency lighting/exit sign circuits campus wide, including backup battery maintenance Troubleshoots, repairs, and maintains access control, door alarms, handi-cap openers, and security camera circuits campus wide Inspects completed work to ensure compliance with engineering specifications, local and NYS\u00a0 codes, and verifies system is realigned for operational readiness Maintains an adequate inventory of parts required for timely repairs Stores and utilizes chemicals and equipment in a safe/compliant manner, including maintaining MSDS sheets Plans scheduled maintenance, creates materials lists, and requisitions materials and equipment Maintains all aspects of electrical/electronic systems at the facilities to comply with NYS Building and Fire Codes Maintains a proper inventory of electrical tools and equipment associated with the trade \u00a0in a good and safe working order per manufacturers recommendations Performs all electrical work assigned in accordance with applicable safety precautions/procedures Communicate with Public Safety and Staff via 2-way radio communication Receive, complete, and submit all work order processing documentation accurately and on time Snow removal using shovels and/or equipment as assigned:\u00a0 May include off hours scheduling in accordance with BSEIU Local 51 Contract All other general maintenance duties as assigned The estimated wage is $26.39\u00a0per hour for 40\u00a0hours per week for 52\u00a0weeks. Requirements: A trade school or vocational high school diploma is required or experience through a recognized apprenticeship program or a combination of both Five years experience as an electrician Must be familiar with various electrical and mechanical systems, including heating and ventilation systems, air conditioning systems, lighting systems, DDC Control systems, fire alarm/sprinkler systems, and telecommunication systems Must have knowledge of communications wiring, equipment and technology.\u00a0 Experience with Lucent Technologies equipment is preferred Must be able to cut, bend, thread and \u00a0fit conduit Must have highly developed electrical ability/aptitude and be familiar with terminology of the trade Must have complete knowledge of materials related to electrical systems Must be able to interpret and follow architectural and general engineering drawings, schematics and specifications as well as manufacturers installation and maintenance documentation Must be able to follow verbal and written instructions Must have a basic knowledge of local and NYS Electrical, Building, and Fire Codes Must be able to lift and carry objects up to 51 lbs without assistance Must be able to work from heights, including mechanical lifting devices Must be able to read instructions and safety rules, write sentences, communicate verbally and follow instructions Must be able to add, subtract, multiply and divide Must be able to walk, stoop, bend, crouch, sit, kneel, climb and crawl Must be able to work independently with minimal supervision Must be available for emergency call-ins Valid NYS driver's license is required Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications accepted until position is filled. Reports to: Senior Director of Facilities Maintenance and Planning Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Resume Cover letter A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=195248": {"title": "HVAC Technician", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: HVAC Technician Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: HVAC Technician Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details HVAC Technician Category: Staff Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Locations: Troy & Albany, NY Posted: Dec 2, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Non-Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 195248 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge.\u00a0Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: This is a full-time, hourly staff position for Russell Sage College (Troy and Albany campuses). Job Summary: Performs major maintenance and repair of HVAC equipment including, but not limited to: water source heat pumps, cooling towers, residential and commercial heating/cooling systems, chillers, and commercial rooftop units. Also provides service and repairs in the areas of preventative maintenance, plumbing, equipment repairs and maintenance, and other duties as assigned. Is knowledgeable of commonly used concepts, practices, and procedures within a particular field. Relies on experience and judgment to perform the functions of the job. Works under limited supervision. A wide degree of creativity and latitude is required. Performs a variety of tasks. Will lead and teach members of Facilities Management, in the field of HVAC repair and preventative maintenance. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Provide labor, skills and expertise, with a primary focus on quality workmanship, the safety, functionality and comfort of students, staff, faculty and visitors Specifically checks and repairs and/or replaces valves, steam traps, motors, controls, switches, gauges, wiring, fans, pumps, compressors, condensers, cores, coils, tube bundles, pipes, heat exchanges, and other functional components of the system. HVAC trouble shooting/installation and repair HVAC on-call required Renovations, construction, repair, lifting, moving, electrical and plumbing. Manages or assists in planning and estimating projects. Responsible for preparation, compiling, proper tracking and filing of daily work orders, supply house packing slips and invoices for supplies Put a preventative maintenance schedule Filter changes Works directly with the Senior Director of Facilities and Planning, Crew Coordinators, and all maintenance staff. Deals with contractors, vendors, regulatory agencies and municipal building code officials. The estimated\u00a0wage is $27.45\u00a0per hour for 40\u00a0hours per week for 52\u00a0weeks. Requirements: Associates degree Licensed and CFC Universal Certification in HVAC Technology Minimum of 5 years of commercial and residential job-related experience, specifically in: HVAC maintenance and repair or CFC Universal Certification in HVAC Technology Minimum of 10 years of commercial and residential job-related experience, specifically in: HVACV maintenance and repair. Must have a NYS drivers license that is in good standing. Experience with working on Carrier Comfort View 6400 software and controls. Must be able to read instructions and safety rules, write sentences, communicate verbally, and follow instructions. Must be able to add, subtract, multiply, and divide. Must be able to frequently lift and carry objects weighing up to 50 lbs. Must be able to walk, stoop, bend, crouch, sit, kneel, climb ladders, and crawl Must be able to work independently with minimum supervision Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications accepted until position is filled. Reports to:\u00a0Senior Director of Facilities and Planning Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Resume Cover letter A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=186658": {"title": "General Maintenance/Housekeeping", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: General Maintenance/Housekeeping Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: General Maintenance/Housekeeping Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details General Maintenance/Housekeeping Category: Staff Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities/ Maintenance Locations: Troy & Albany, NY Posted: Mar 24, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Non-Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 186658 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge.\u00a0Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: Job Summary :\u00a0 Generally responsible for cleaning of all buildings and common areas of the campus and in assisting with repairs and maintenance of the College. This position is for either the Troy or Albany campus; specific schedule to be determined with supervisor. Assists with general repairs and maintenance as required by the Crew Coordinator or Senior Director of Facilities and Planning Cleans and maintains cleanliness of all areas used by College community Collects and disposes of trash and debris Utilizes chemicals and equipment in a safe/compliant manner Clear pathways and parking lots of snow using shovels and/or equipment as assigned Other responsibilities as assigned by the Crew Coordinator or Senior Director of Facilities and Planning May include one or more of the following: Delivery of merchandise from shipping/receiving area Assisting with the grounds upkeep Assisting skilled workers in the area of carpentry, painting, masonry or electrical Assist in some aspects of building repair including changing light bulbs, fuses and ballasts Replace window shades, light painting, assist in grounds as needed Sweeps, mops and scrubs, strips floors, stairs and other surfaces Vacuums and spot cleans carpets Cleans and restocks lavatories Collects trash and debris and places in designated collection area for removal by Waste Collector Replaces liners in wastebaskets and trash containers Cleans stoves, microwaves and refrigerators as directed Cleans or dusts glass and other exposed surfaces including walls, window sills, cases, phone booths, door trim, chalkboards and furniture Sweeps porches, steps and sidewalks to clear debris and snowfall and applies ice melt as required Reports all hazardous conditions to the appropriate supervisor especially as it relates to snow removal Removes snow as requested by supervisor Reports items in need of repair to the appropriate supervisor Maintains equipment in clean, usable condition Uses cleaning chemicals in a responsible manner Ensures chemicals are safely and properly stored after each use and that correct labels are applied Moves furniture, supplies and miscellaneous equipment as directed Maintains floor finishes In emergency situation, may be directed to clean up spills, floods and other related items All other duties related to custodial work as assigned This is a 12-month position with a\u00a0starting wage of\u00a0$18.00 per hour for 40 hours per week. Applications are accepted and reviewed on an ongoing basis. Requirements: At least 1 year experience in housekeeping general building repair, maintenance Must be able to follow oral and written instructions Must be able to push and lift and carry objects up to 51 lbs without assistance Must be able to read instructions and safety rules, write sentences, communicate verbally and follow instructions Must be able to add, subtract, multiply and divide Must be able to walk, stoop, bend, crouch, sit, kneel, climb and crawl Valid NYS driver's license is required Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications accepted and reviewed on an ongoing\u00a0basis. Reports to:\u00a0Group Leader and Senior Director Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Resume Cover letter A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=177954": {"title": "Housekeeper", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: Housekeeper Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: Housekeeper Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Housekeeper Category: Staff Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Housekeeping Locations: Albany and/or Troy, NY Posted: Jun 20, 2024 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Non-Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 177954 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge.\u00a0Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: Job Summary: Generally responsible for cleaning of all buildings and common areas of the campus RESPONSIBILITIES: Cleans and maintains cleanliness of all areas used by College community Collects and disposes of trash and debris Utilizes chemicals and equipment in a sensible manner Other responsibilities as assigned by the Housekeeping Supervisor, Crew Coordinator or Senior Director of Facilities. DUTIES: Sweeps, mops and scrubs floors, stairs and other surfaces Cleans, services and restocks lavatories Collects trash and debris and places in designated collection area for removal by Waste Collector Replaces liners in wastebaskets and trash containers Cleans stoves, microwaves and refrigerators as directed Cleans or dusts glass and other exposed surfaces including walls, window sills, cases, phone booths, door trim, chalkboards and furniture Sweeps porches, steps and sidewalks to clear debris and snowfall and applies ice melt as required Reports all hazardous conditions to the appropriate supervisor especially as it relates to snow removal Reports items in need of repair to the appropriate supervisor Maintains equipment in clean, usable condition Uses cleaning chemicals in a responsible manner Ensures chemicals are safely and properly stored after each use and that correct labels are applied Moves furniture, supplies and miscellaneous equipment as directed Maintains floor finishes In emergency situation, may be directed to clean up spills, floods and other related items All other duties related to custodial work as assigned The estimated\u00a0wage\u00a0is $17.20 per hour for 40\u00a0hours per week for 52\u00a0weeks. *For certain shifts, there may be a shift differential. Applications are reviewed on an ongoing basis. This role will be on the Albany or Troy campus, including work on the Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences campus. Specific shifts may vary. Requirements: At least 1 year experience in housekeeping/janitorial services, preferably in a residence or similar environment Must be able to follow oral and written instructions Must be able to push and lift a maximum of 20 lbs Must be able to read instructions and safety rules, write sentences, communicate verbally and follow instructions Must be able to add, subtract, multiply and divide Must be able to walk, stoop, bend, crouch, sit, kneel, climb, reach and crawl Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere along with opportunities for tuition waiver, employer matched retirement plan for eligible employees and many other benefits.\u00a0 For complete employee benefit information, please visit our Employee Benefits page. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications are reviewed on an ongoing basis. Reports to: Housekeeping Supervisor Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Resume Cover letter A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204088": {"title": "Medical Assistant", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: Medical Assistant Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: Medical Assistant Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Medical Assistant Category: Staff Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Wellness Center Locations: Albany/ Troy, NY Posted: Aug 25, 2026 Closes: Dec 4, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Full-time Position\u00a0ID: 204088 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge. Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: Position Summary: The Medical Assistant is a nine-month position (40 weeks) that reports to the Associate Vice President for Student Life and Dean for Wellness providing both clinical and administrative support to ensure the efficient delivery of high-quality healthcare services to students. In collaboration with the Wellness Center's medical providers, the Medical Assistant assists with patient care, clinical procedures, front office operations, medical records management, and health service administration. Responsibilities include but are not limited to: Prepare students for medical examinations by obtaining and documenting medical histories, chief complaints, medications, allergies, vital signs, and other relevant health information. Assist the Nurse Practitioner and other medical providers during examinations, treatments, procedures, and minor surgical interventions. Perform venipuncture, specimen collection, point-of-care testing, and other approved laboratory procedures within scope of practice. Collect, label, process, and prepare laboratory specimens for testing and transport. Administer routine clinical tests as directed by the medical provider. Prepare examination and treatment rooms before and after patient visits. ? Clean, disinfect, sterilize, and maintain medical instruments and equipment in accordance with infection control standards. Ensure examination rooms are fully stocked with appropriate medical supplies and equipment. Provide students with instructions regarding medications, laboratory testing, follow-up appointments, and treatment plans as directed by the medical provider. Observe and report changes in patient condition to the medical provider. Assist in responding to urgent medical situations within the Wellness Center. Perform front desk operations, including greeting students and visitors in a professional and welcoming manner. Answer incoming telephone calls and respond appropriately to student inquiries. Schedule, confirm, and manage student appointments. Complete patient registration, check-in, and check-out procedures. Verify and update demographic, insurance, and medical information. Assist with referrals to specialists, laboratories, diagnostic services, and community healthcare providers. Process laboratory requests and maintain laboratory tracking records. Maintain accurate patient records while ensuring compliance with HIPAA, FERPA, and institutional confidentiality standards. Scan, file, and organize medical documentation in accordance with record retention policies. Assist with correspondence, reports, and administrative projects as assigned. Monitor inventory levels of medical supplies, medications,laboratory materials, and clinical equipment. Order and restock medical supplies as needed. Maintain organized and properly stocked examination and treatment rooms. Assist with quality assurance activities and equipment maintenance. Ensure compliance with infection prevention, OSHA, and biohazard disposal regulations. Report equipment malfunctions Provide compassionate, respectful, and culturally responsive customer service to students. Assist students in navigating Wellness Center services and appointment procedures. Maintain a welcoming and inclusive clinical environment. Promote student privacy and dignity during all interactions. Provide health education materials and reinforce provider instructions. Maintain strict confidentiality of all student health information in accordance with HIPAA, FERPA, and College policies. Follow established infection control, safety, and emergency procedures. Ensure compliance with OSHA, CDC, New York State Department of Health, and institutional regulations. Collaborate with the Wellness Center team, Accessibility Services, Recreation and Fitness, Athletics, and other student support offices to coordinate holistic care. Participate in Wellness Center staff meetings and departmental initiatives. Support campus health promotion events, vaccination clinics, and wellness programming. Actively contributes, participates and supports Thrive programming and initiatives Maintain required certifications and competencies. Perform other duties as assigned by the Associate Vice President for Student Life and Dean for Wellness. The estimated wage is $22.23\u00a0per hour for 37.5 hours per week for 40\u00a0weeks. Requirements: High school degree required Completion of an accredited medical assistance program recommended Two years of medical assistant experience recommended. Previous experience performing venipuncture, blood draws, specimen collection, and basic laboratory procedures Excellent interpersonal skills Ability to communicate clearly and effectively with patients and other external parties in a courteous and friendly manner at all times Must be detail-oriented and highly organized Knowledge of patient care and examination procedures Must be able to maintain confidentiality at all times Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications accepted until position is filled. Reports to:\u00a0Associate Vice President for Student Life and Dean for Wellness Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Resume Cover letter A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203606": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor - Microbiology and Anatomy & Physiology", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor - Microbiology and Anatomy & Physiology Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor - Microbiology and Anatomy & Physiology Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor - Microbiology and Anatomy & Physiology Category: Adjunct Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Biology and Health Sciences Locations: Troy, NY Posted: Aug 12, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Contract Position\u00a0ID: 203606 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge. Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: Russell Sage College is seeking an adjunct instructor to teach a section of Microbiology lab during the Fall 2026 semester. The section is on Wednesday morning at 9:30 , and is full with no chance of being cancelled. This position offers the opportunity to contribute to the success of students preparing for careers in healthcare and STEM by providing a strong foundation in chemical principles and laboratory skills. ***************************************** RSC also is looking for an adjunct\u00a0to cover two\u00a0labs in Anatomy and Physiology : Tues 5 PM - 7:50 PM Thurs 1 PM- \u00a03:50 PM Helpful information from the catalog: First term: Students will investigate the structure and function of the cell, the skeletal and neuromuscular systems, and the proprioceptive and reticular activating systems relative to sensation, perception, and movement. Second term: Studies of the blood, circulatory, digestive, and urinary systems will be included. Laboratory work will include experiments on animals and animal tissue and exercises with human subjects. Students who take this course cannot receive credit for BIO 213. **************************************** Adjunct compensation is currently $1,000 per credit hour (depending on staffing needs and enrollment). Requirements: A graduate degree in biology, an MA or MS is acceptable . Experience working with students in nursing, health sciences, or other STEM programs is desirable. Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications accepted until position is filled. Reports to: Biology & Health Sciences Department Chair Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Resume Cover letter A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203074": {"title": "General Chemistry Lecture & Laboratory Adjunct Instructor", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: General Chemistry Lecture & Laboratory Adjunct Instructor Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: General Chemistry Lecture & Laboratory Adjunct Instructor Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details General Chemistry Lecture & Laboratory Adjunct Instructor Category: Adjunct Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Chemistry, Physics, and Mathematics Locations: Troy, NY Posted: Jul 28, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position\u00a0ID: 203074 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge. Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: Russell Sage College is seeking an adjunct instructor to teach one section of CHM 111: General Chemistry Lecture and two sections of CHM 103L: Introduction to General Chemistry Labs during the Fall 2026 semester. The instructor will be responsible for delivering engaging lecture instruction and facilitating laboratory experiences that reinforce core chemical principles while promoting scientific inquiry, critical thinking, and laboratory safety. There is a possibility to extend the position to Spring 2027 to teach a section of CHM 103 Labs. This position offers the opportunity to contribute to the success of students preparing for careers in healthcare and STEM by providing a strong foundation in chemical principles and laboratory skills. Course topics include atomic structure, chemical bonding, stoichiometry, states of matter, solutions, thermochemistry, chemical equilibrium, acids and bases, oxidation-reduction reactions, and an introduction to organic and biochemistry concepts. Laboratory instruction emphasizes safe laboratory practices, data collection and analysis, scientific communication, and the application of chemical concepts through hands-on experimentation. Adjunct compensation is currently $1,000 per credit hour (depending on staffing needs and enrollment). Requirements: A graduate degree in chemistry with previous experience teaching college-level chemistry lectures and/or laboratories. Experience working with students in nursing, health sciences, or other STEM programs is desirable. Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications accepted until position is filled. Reports to: Chair of the Chemistry, Physics & Mathematics Department Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Resume Cover letter A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=195037": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor for Mathematics for Teaching and Learning II", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor for Mathematics for Teaching and Learning II Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor for Mathematics for Teaching and Learning II Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor for Mathematics for Teaching and Learning II Category: Adjunct Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Chemistry, Physics & Mathematics Locations: Troy, NY Posted: Nov 21, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position\u00a0ID: 195037 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge.\u00a0Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: Russell Sage College is seeking an adjunct instructor to teach MAT 121: Mathematics for Teaching and Learning II during the Spring 2026 semester. This course builds on foundational concepts introduced in MAT 111 and deepens understanding of mathematical ideas essential for effective teaching. The course aligns with the New York State Next Generation Learning Standards, covering Expressions & Equations, Algebra, Geometry, Measurement & Data, and Statistics & Probability. Enrollment is limited to Childhood and Middle Childhood Education majors, with an emphasis on developing strong conceptual understanding, procedural fluency, and the ability to design meaningful, student-centered mathematics learning environments. Adjunct compensation is currently $1000 per credit hour (depending on staffing needs and enrollment). Requirements: A master's degree or higher in mathematics, mathematics education, education, or a closely related field is required. Preference will be given to candidates with experience teaching mathematics to pre-service teachers or at the elementary, middle childhood, or secondary level. Familiarity with the New York State Next Generation Learning Standards and evidence-based, student-centered mathematics instruction is strongly preferred. Experience teaching undergraduate courses and supporting diverse learners in inclusive learning environments is desirable. Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications accepted until position is filled. Reports to: Chair of the Chemistry, Physics & Mathematics Department Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Resume Cover letter A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact 