aff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: The Department of Visual & Performing Arts (art.sage.edu) at Russell Sage College (sage.edu) seeks applications for teaching positions in our NASAD-accredited Expressive Arts in Mental Health (BS) program, course title: Art Therapy Communication .\u00a0Ideal candidates will have their NY Licensed Creative Arts Therapist (LCAT), diverse clinical experience, and previous teaching experience. Accredited since 1978 by the National Association of Schools of Art and Design (NASAD), Russell Sage College offers numerous creative degrees in visual and performing arts including Art + Extended Media (BFA), Interior + Spatial Design (BFA), Graphic + Media Design (BFA), Expressive Arts in Mental Health (BS), Musical Theatre (BS), and Theatre (BA). Adjunct compensation is currently $1000 per credit hour (depending on staffing needs and enrollment). Requirements: Master's degree in Art Therapy, Registration or Board Certification (ATR or ATR-BC) by the American Art Therapy Association, NY state licensure as LCAT (Licensed Creative Arts Therapist) or LMHC (Licensed Mental Health Counselor). Ideal candidates will be a NY Licensed Creative Arts Therapist (LCAT), have college-level teaching experience, and a diverse clinical background. Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications accepted until position is filled. Reports to: Expressive Arts in Mental Health Program Director Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Resume Cover letter A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=183430": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Graphic Design", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Graphic Design Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Graphic Design Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of Graphic Design Category: Adjunct Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Visual & Performing Arts Locations: Albany, NY Posted: Nov 25, 2024 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position\u00a0ID: 183430 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge.\u00a0Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: The Department of Visual & Performing Arts (art.sage.edu) at Russell Sage College (sage.edu) seeks applications for teaching positions in our NASAD-accredited Graphic + Media Design BFA program. Ideal candidates will have professional experience working in graphic design, typography, digital imaging, web design, UI/UX, motion graphics, animation, and/or video production/editing. Accredited since 1978 by the National Association of Schools of Art and Design (NASAD), Russell Sage College offers numerous creative degrees in visual and performing arts including Art + Extended Media (BFA), Interior + Spatial Design (BFA), Graphic + Media Design (BFA), Expressive Arts in Mental Health (BS), Musical Theatre (BS), and Theatre (BA). Adjunct compensation is currently $1000 per credit hour (depending on staffing needs and enrollment) Requirements: Bachelor's or master's degree in graphic design, visual communications, new media, or related field, and demonstrated knowledge of design-related technology is required. College-level teaching experience and a significant record of professional art/design activity are preferred. Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications accepted until position is filled. Reports to: Chair of the Visual & Performing Arts Department Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Curriculum Vitae Three professional references (name, title, phone number, email address) Examples of professional work as a\u00a0multi-page PDF or website Examples of student\u00a0work (if applicable) as a\u00a0multi-page PDF or website Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=183429": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Interior Design", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Interior Design Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Interior Design Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of Interior Design Category: Adjunct Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Visual & Performing Arts Locations: Albany, NY Posted: Nov 25, 2024 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position\u00a0ID: 183429 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge.\u00a0Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: The Department of Visual & Performing Arts (art.sage.edu) at Russell Sage College (sage.edu) seeks applications for a teaching position in our robust, NASAD-accredited Interior + Spatial Design BFA program. Ideal candidates will be interested and able to teach interior design principles, perspective and rendering, computer-aided design, materials and applications, lighting, building systems & codes, history of architecture, and/or sustainable building design to prepare students for CIDA and NCIDQ certification. Accredited since 1978 by the National Association of Schools of Art and Design (NASAD), Russell Sage College offers numerous creative degrees in visual and performing arts including Art + Extended Media (BFA), Interior + Spatial Design (BFA), Graphic + Media Design (BFA), Expressive Arts in Mental Health (BS), Musical Theatre (BS), and Theatre (BA). Adjunct compensation is currently $1000 per credit hour (depending on staffing needs and enrollment). Requirements: Required:\u00a0MS or MFA degree preferred with at least one degree in interior design. Applicants with a BFA degree must demonstrate equivalent working experience and demonstrated knowledge of interior design practices. College-level teaching experience and availability to teach day and evening classes preferred. Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications accepted until position is filled. Reports to: Chair of the Visual & Performing Arts Department Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Curriculum Vitae Three professional references (name, title, phone number, email address) Examples of professional work as a\u00a0multi-page PDF or website Examples of student\u00a0work (if applicable) as a\u00a0multi-page PDF or website Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application. Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=183426": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Management", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Management Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Management Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of Management Category: Adjunct Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Management Locations: Albany, NY Posted: Nov 25, 2024 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position\u00a0ID: 183426 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge.\u00a0Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: The Department of Management at Russell Sage College is seeking qualified, motivated, and dynamic Adjunct Faculty members to teach a variety of courses across different disciplines at both the undergraduate and graduate level.\u00a0 Adjunct faculty will be responsible for providing high-quality instruction and engaging with students to foster a positive learning environment.\u00a0 Various disciplines include, but not necessarily limited to, the following: Finance & Accounting Digital Marketing Business Strategy Economics Leadership & Ethics Quality Management Human Resource Management & Organizational Behavior Project Management Healthcare Strategy Legal Aspects of Healthcare Administration The ideal candidates should possess a strong background in their respective fields and demonstrate a commitment to teaching excellence, student success, and continuous professional development. Key Responsibilities: Prepare and deliver high-quality undergraduate and graduate-level instruction aligned with established curriculum and learning objectives. Create a supportive and interactive classroom environment, in-person, livestream, or online as applicable. Facilitate engaging discussions and case studies that integrate practical business experiences with academic theory. Access and evaluate student progress through assignments, exams, and projects, and provide constructive feedback. Provide timely feedback to students and be accessible to address their concerns or questions. Maintain accurate records of student attendance, grades, and performance. Participate in department meetings, professional development, and relevant institutional activities as required. Collaborate with Program Directors to ensure course objectives are met. Stay current with developments in your field and integrate new knowledge into teaching practice. Follow all institutional policies and procedures, including grading deadlines and academic integrity guidelines. Work Conditions: Flexible schedule based on course offerings. Contract is for evening classes. Adjunct compensation is currently $1000 per credit hour (depending on staffing needs and enrollment) Requirements: Minimum Education Requirement: Master's degree or higher in the relevant discipline from an accredited institution.\u00a0 (Doctorate preferred for some disciplines). Teaching Experience: Prior teaching experience, particularly at the college and/or university level, is preferred. Familiarity with different teaching modalities, including in-person, livestream, and online. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to work effectively with a diverse student population. Additional Information: RSC offers a dynamic college environment and friendly work atmosphere. Visit our Employment Opportunities page for additional available job openings at RSC. Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Reports to: Department Chair/Program Director Application Instructions: If you are interested in applying for this position, please submit the following documents by clicking on the APPLY NOW button and follow the steps. Current curriculum vitae (CV) or resume Cover letter detailing relevant teaching and business experience A list of three professional references (Name, phone number, email address etc.) Unofficial Transcripts (official transcripts required upon hiring). Please Note: After submitting your Resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your cover letter and any additional documents you wish to send. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Sage Colleges Careers Account to check your completed application.Send letter of application, resume, and list of three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=79042": {"title": "Nursing Adjunct Faculty", "description": "Russell Sage College\nJob Posting: Nursing Adjunct Faculty Russell Sage College \n\tJob Posting: Nursing Adjunct Faculty Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Nursing Adjunct Faculty Category: Adjunct Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing Locations: Troy, NY Posted: Nov 21, 2016 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Temporary Position\u00a0ID: 79042 Share About Russell Sage College: Russell Sage College is a dynamic, comprehensive college which serves traditional students and working professionals who pursue bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees on campuses in Troy and Albany, NY. Many online programs are also offered. Creating one of the region's largest private higher education institutions with the broadest catalog of programs in the health professions and strong programs in education, business, criminal justice, the sciences, pre-med, pre-health, and arts and humanities, Russell Sage College and Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences (ACPHS) plan to merge.\u00a0Russell Sage and ACPHS will collaborate over the next several years to create a plan to merge their academic portfolios and develop a facilities and people strategy, addressing workforce needs. Russell Sage College offers its faculty and staff the opportunity to make a difference every day - in the lives of students and the future of our communities. Job Description: The Department of Nursing at Russell\u00a0Sage College\u00a0is seeking highly-motivated adjunct faculty who are interested in teaching undergraduate or graduate theory in class, hybrid or online courses; onsite campus clinical and simulation labs; and clinical rotations in a variety of acute and community health settings, and/or conducting site visits for Nurse Practitioner (NP). Adjunct compensation is currently $1000 per credit hour (depending on staffing needs and enrollment). Requirements: Minimum adjunct faculty qualifications include: Master's (or higher degree) in Nursing; Current clinical expertise relevant to the course content or specific lab or clinical rotation; Current licensure as a Registered Nurse in New York State. If a candidate is applying to teach in the graduate NP Program and/or conducting clinical site visits for NP students, current national NP certification is required. Preference will be given to candidates who also have prior theory or clinical teaching experience and familiarity with Moodle (or a similar learning platform). Additional Information: Russell Sage College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against otherwise qualified applicants on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, ancestry, age, sex, marital status, national origin, disability, veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, pregnancy, gender, gender identity or expression, familial status, status as a victim of domestic violence, reproductive health decision making, criminal history, and any other legally protected characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In this regard, opportunities for advancement will be made available without bias. The College is also subject to state and federal laws, supports efforts to attract and retain fully qualified women and other minority group members for faculty and other positions. Russell Sage College will comply with the letter and intent of all State and Federal laws and applicable orders pursuant to Equal Employment Opportunity. Applications will be accepted on an ongoing basis to fill needs each semester Application Instructions: Please upload- by clicking the APPLY NOW button below-\u00a0 a cover letter, current CV, and a list of three professional references. In addition, candidates should ensure their professional letters of reference are written and uploaded to Interview Exchange in a timely manner. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Russell Sage College - Troy Campus 65 1st Street, Troy, NY 12180"}}, "rows": {"https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205154": {"school_id": 1015, "posting_url": "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205154", "job_title_in_post": "Administrative Assistant", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205200": {"school_id": 1015, "posting_url": "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205200", "job_title_in_post": "Major Gifts Officer", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205245": {"school_id": 1015, "posting_url": "https://sage.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205245", "job_title_in_post": "Administrative Offic